-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Bucks County came in under 90% of normal in August to September for 36 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair ran 50% of normal on the middle of the grids, and January to February matched it at 50%. So far in 2026 the middle of the grids sits at 67% for April to May and 95% for June to July. Every grid had its driest year in 1965, with grid 24521 at 63%.</p>"}
